{# THE ZONES SECTION OF AN AREA'S CONFIGURE PAGE — the set is changed here and
   nowhere else, and the Zones tab is where it is read.

   Design: areas/<area>/configure-zones.html.

   THE SPLIT IS THE INCIDENT DETAIL PAGE'S, unchanged: the shell's own
   `.recgrid` — a wide column beside a narrow one, 16px between them. LEFT, the
   plate and the zones, whose cards are full-row and open in place. RIGHT, the
   import card and the log, which keeps the sidebar alive when nothing is being
   previewed.

   NO PAGE-LEVEL SAVE anywhere. A rename, a ring and an import each commit from
   their own control, so there is one form per write and no form around the page.

   THE STATE OF THE IMPORT CARD IS THE DATA'S. An area with no zones gets the
   first-import card; an area with zones gets the resting one; a plan held from
   a preview replaces both; a file that could not be read shows its refusal. The
   design's state switcher is a design tool and has no counterpart here.

   AN OPEN CARD'S BODY is what the modules publish about that ground over a
   rolling window, then the stations standing on it — one card per station, with who
   is there and the way through to its record — and a footer strip stating how
   many of the zone's stations were drawn. A zone has no people of its own: it
   has the ground its stations stand on, which is why the people are read per
   station and never as a zone-level list. #}
{% extends '@Shell/page.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}{{ area.name }} · configure · zones{% endblock %}

{% block stylesheets %}
    {{ parent() }}
    {{ include('@Area/_stylesheets.html.twig') }}
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_breadcrumbs %}
    <a href="{{ path('area_index') }}">uhifadhi</a> / <a href="{{ path('area_show', {uuid: area.uuidString}) }}">{{ area.name }}</a> / configure / zones
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_title %}{{ area.name }} &middot; configure{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_subtitle %}The zone set is changed here &mdash; imported, named, added to; the <b>Zones</b> tab is where it is read.{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_actions %}
    {# TAB-SPECIFIC ACTIONS SIT TO THE LEFT OF CONFIGURE, which the frame writes
       itself at the right-hand end of every area page. #}
    <a class="cta" href="{{ path('area_zones', {uuid: area.uuidString}) }}">Open Zones {{ ux_icon('shell:arrow-right') }}</a>
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page %}
{% set section = path('area_zones_configure', {uuid: area.uuidString}) %}
<div class="recgrid">
    <div class="col">
        {# THE HOUSE MAP CONTRACT, and nothing on this plate is drawn
           differently: the atlas draws the boundary with its scrim, the rings in
           one layer, the controls where every other map in the product puts
           them, and the key BELOW the plate — here the zone key, since hue is
           the zone. #}
        <div class="c">
            {% if plan %}
                <span class="tab">Preview<span class="src">&middot; the zones this file carries</span></span>
            {% elseif set.isEmpty %}
                <span class="tab">Preview<span class="src">&middot; the boundary, and nothing in it yet</span></span>
            {% else %}
                <span class="tab">Preview<span class="src">&middot; the zones on the ground</span></span>
            {% endif %}
            {{ render_map(map, {
                'role': 'img',
                'aria-label': plan
                    ? 'The zones ' ~ plan.fileName ~ ' would add, drawn on ' ~ area.name
                    : area.name ~ ' and its zones',
            }) }}
        </div>

        {# THE SPINE. One card per zone, full row in a flex stack: a card that
           opens must never sit in a grid, or opening it pushes its neighbours. #}
        <div class="c">
            {% if set.isEmpty %}
                <span class="tab">The zones<span class="src">&middot; none yet</span></span>
                <div class="deptgroup">
                    <span class="gh">The set</span>
                    <span class="gc">0</span>
                    <span class="gnote">0{% if set.groundKm2 %} of {{ set.groundKm2|number_format }}{% endif %} km&sup2;</span>
                    <span class="gl"></span>
                </div>
                <div class="zempty"><b class="zeh">No zones yet</b><span class="zemono">import a file, or draw one</span></div>
            {% else %}
                <span class="tab">The zones<span class="src">&middot; {{ set.count }} &middot; open one, rename, or add one</span></span>
                <div class="deptgroup">
                    <span class="gh">The set</span>
                    <span class="gc">{{ set.count }}</span>
                    <span class="gnote">
                        {%- if set.lastImport -%}
                            last import <time datetime="{{ set.lastImport.importedAt|date('c') }}" data-localtime-format="day">{{ set.lastImport.importedAt|date('j M Y') }}</time>
                            {%- if set.lastImport.importedBy %} by {{ set.lastImport.importedBy }}{% endif %}
                            &middot; names from <code>{{ set.lastImport.nameProperty }}</code> &middot;
                        {%- endif -%}
                        {{ set.zonedKm2|number_format }}{% if set.groundKm2 %} of {{ set.groundKm2|number_format }}{% endif %} km&sup2;
                    </span>
                    <span class="gl"></span>
                </div>

                <div class="zcstack">
                    {% for row in set.rows %}
                        {% set isOpen = openZone == row.uuid %}
                        {# A NATIVE DISCLOSURE, the twin of the stations register's
                           card. Opening a zone used to be a NAVIGATION —
                           `?open=<uuid>`, a round trip and a repaint to reveal
                           markup the page could have carried — and the reload is
                           what a reader notices. `<details>` opens it in the
                           browser, with no script to ship and keyboard and
                           screen-reader support already right.

                           THE SERVER STILL DECIDES WHAT ARRIVES OPEN: `?open=`
                           renders `open` on the card it names, so a link into a
                           zone still lands on it.

                           THE RENAME DISCLOSURE MOVED INTO THE BODY. It used to
                           sit in the header, and a `<details>` inside a
                           `<summary>` is invalid markup whose one certain
                           behaviour is that clicking it toggles the card. An
                           edit belongs in the open card anyway, which is where
                           the stations twin keeps its own. #}
                        <details class="zcard{{ isOpen ? ' on focusline' : '' }}"{{ isOpen ? ' open' : '' }}>
                            <summary class="zc-hd">
                                <span class="ovx" aria-hidden="true">{{ ux_icon('shell:chevron-right') }}</span>
                                <span class="zsw" data-cat="{{ row.cat }}"></span>
                                <div class="zc-bd">
                                    <span class="nmrow"><a class="zc-nm" href="{{ path('area_zones', {uuid: area.uuidString}) }}">{{ row.name }}</a></span>
                                </div>
                                {# THE RUN IS READ WITH THE CARD SHUT, so nought is a word and not a
                                   measurement: "no station" says a thing about the ground, where
                                   "0 st" reads as something that was counted wrong. #}
                                {% set covered = figures.covered(row.uuid) %}
                                {% set posts = staffing.stationsIn(row.uuid) %}
                                {% set people = staffing.peopleIn(row.uuid) %}
                                <span class="zcrun">
                                    <span class="f"><b>{{ row.km2|number_format }}</b> km&sup2;</span>
                                    {% if row.shareOfArea is not null %}<span class="f"><b>{{ row.shareOfArea }}</b>%</span>{% endif %}
                                    {% if covered %}<span class="f"><b>{{ covered.display }}</b>{{ covered.unit }} covered</span>{% endif %}
                                    <span class="f">{% if posts %}<b>{{ posts }}</b> st{% else %}no station{% endif %}</span>
                                    <span class="f">{% if people %}<b>{{ people }}</b> stationed{% else %}nobody stationed{% endif %}</span>
                                </span>
                            </summary>

                                <hr class="zc-rule">

                                {# RENAME COMMITS ON ITS OWN — it touches no geometry, so it needs
                                   neither the map nor a file — and it sits behind a disclosure.
                                   A field and a button in every collapsed card's header made the
                                   header twice the height the design draws and turned a list of
                                   eleven zones into a column of forms. #}
                                <details class="zc-act dc-more">
                                    <summary class="btn sm">{{ ux_icon('shell:square-pen') }} Rename &#9662;</summary>
                                    <div class="dc-panel">
                                        <form method="post" action="{{ path('area_zone_rename', {uuid: area.uuidString, zone: row.uuid}) }}">
                                            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ renameToken }}">
                                            <label class="sbf grow"><span class="k">Name</span>
                                                <input class="fld" type="text" name="name" value="{{ row.name }}" maxlength="128" aria-label="Rename {{ row.name }}">
                                            </label>
                                            <button type="submit" class="btn sm">Save the name</button>
                                        </form>
                                    </div>
                                </details>

                                {# WHAT THE MODULES PUBLISH ABOUT THIS GROUND, over the rolling
                                   window the controller asked for. The covered share is already in
                                   the run above, so it is not drawn twice; a zone nobody publishes
                                   about draws no row at all rather than a line of dashes. #}
                                {% set zonefigs = figures.forZone(row.uuid)|filter(figure => figure.key != constant('Uhifadhi\\Contracts\\Kpi\\ZoneFigureProviderInterface::COVERED')) %}
                                {% if zonefigs is not empty %}
                                    <div class="zcfigs">
                                        {% for figure in zonefigs %}
                                            <span class="f"><b>{{ figure.display }}</b>{{ figure.unit }} {{ figure.label|lower }}</span>
                                        {% endfor %}
                                        <span class="q">{{ figures.period.label }}</span>
                                    </div>
                                {% endif %}

                                {# THE STATIONS ON THIS GROUND. A zone has no people of its own — it has
                                   the ground its stations stand on — so the people are read here per
                                   station and never as a zone-level list. Manage people NAVIGATES to
                                   the station's own record, which is the surface that edits assignments. #}
                                <div class="stgroup">
                                    <div class="stgh">
                                        <span class="zsw" data-cat="{{ row.cat }}"></span>
                                        <b>{{ row.name }}</b>
                                        <span class="stghm">
                                            {{- row.km2|number_format }} km&sup2;
                                            {%- if covered %} &middot; {{ covered.display }}{{ covered.unit }} covered{% endif -%}
                                            {{ ' ' }}&middot; {{ people }} {{ people == 1 ? 'person' : 'people' -}}
                                        </span>
                                    </div>
                                    {% if stationCards is empty %}
                                        <div class="stcard none">
                                            <b>No station stands in this zone</b>
                                            <span class="stnone">ordinary &middot; a station is recorded in the Stations section</span>
                                        </div>
                                    {% else %}
                                        <div class="stcards">
                                            {% for card in stationCards %}
                                                <div class="stcard{{ card.posted ? '' : ' empty' }}">
                                                    <div class="stcardhd">
                                                        <span class="stpin{{ card.posted ? '' : ' hollow' }}">{{ card.posted }}</span>
                                                        <b>{{ card.name }}</b>
                                                        {% if card.code %}<span class="stcode">{{ card.code }}</span>{% endif %}
                                                    </div>
                                                    <div class="stcardppl{{ card.posted ? '' : ' empty' }}">
                                                        {% if card.faces is not empty %}
                                                            <span class="avstack">
                                                                {%- for face in card.faces -%}
                                                                    <span class="tav sm" title="{{ face.name }}{% if face.role %} &middot; {{ face.role }}{% endif %}">{{ face.initials|slice(0, 1) }}</span>
                                                                {%- endfor -%}
                                                                {%- if card.beyondTheFaces %}<span class="tav sm more">+{{ card.beyondTheFaces }}</span>{% endif -%}
                                                            </span>
                                                        {% endif %}
                                                        <span class="stcardlead">
                                                            {%- if card.leaderName %}{{ card.leaderName }} leads &middot; {{ card.posted }} posted
                                                            {%- elseif card.posted %}{{ card.posted }} posted &middot; no lead appointed
                                                            {%- else %}nobody stationed yet{% endif -%}
                                                        </span>
                                                    </div>
                                                    <div class="stcardfoot">
                                                        <span class="mono d">in {{ row.name }}</span>
                                                        <a class="btn sm" href="{{ path('area_station_show', {uuid: area.uuidString, station: card.uuid}) }}"
                                                           title="{{ card.name }} &middot; stationed people">Manage people &rarr;</a>
                                                    </div>
                                                </div>
                                            {% endfor %}
                                        </div>
                                    {% endif %}
                                </div>

                                <div class="zcmore">
                                    <span class="mono">{{ stationCards|length }} of {{ posts }} {{ posts == 1 ? 'station' : 'stations' }}</span>
                                    {# THE SAME VALIDATION PATH AS AN IMPORT — inside the boundary,
                                       sharing interior with no sibling, this zone excluded from its
                                       own check. A DRAWN ring is the other way in and needs a draw
                                       mode on the atlas plate, which AtlasBundle does not have yet;
                                       its destination is the plate controller in
                                       AtlasBundle/assets/controllers/, writing through this route. #}
                                    <form class="zc-ring" method="post" enctype="multipart/form-data"
                                          action="{{ path('area_zone_ring', {uuid: area.uuidString, zone: row.uuid}) }}">
                                        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ ringToken }}">
                                        <input type="file" class="fld zc-ringfld" name="zones"
                                               accept=".geojson,.json,application/geo+json,application/json"
                                               aria-label="A single-feature file for {{ row.name }}">
                                        <button type="submit" class="btn sm" title="Replace the ring — one polygon, through the same checks">{{ ux_icon('shell:rotate-ccw') }} Replace the ring</button>
                                    </form>
                                    {# DESTRUCTIVE, SO IT ASKS — through the installation's reusable
                                       confirm-modal controller, never the browser's own dialog and
                                       never a page state of this module's invention. The button is
                                       the form's own submit, so an installation that ships no
                                       controller still stations, with the token, and loses nothing but
                                       the question. #}
                                    <form method="post" action="{{ path('area_zone_remove', {uuid: area.uuidString, zone: row.uuid}) }}">
                                        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ removeToken }}">
                                        <button type="submit" class="btn sm dg"
                                                {{ stimulus_controller('confirm-modal') }}
                                                data-action="click->confirm-modal#ask"
                                                data-confirm-modal-title-value="Remove “{{ row.name }}”?"
                                                data-confirm-modal-message-value="Its ground becomes unzoned, which is legal — an area is often only partly zoned. No station, person or record is deleted, and past figures regroup because they were always grouped by geometry."
                                                data-confirm-modal-confirm-label-value="Remove the zone"
                                                data-confirm-modal-danger-value="true">{{ ux_icon('shell:trash-2') }} Remove the zone</button>
                                    </form>
                                </div>
                        </details>
                    {% endfor %}
                </div>
            {% endif %}
            <div class="use">A person is stationed at a <b>station</b>, never to a zone.</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col">
        {# ONE CARD, THE STATES BELOW, AND THE MODEL HELD HERE.

           IMPORT IS ADDITIVE and never overwrites. An empty area takes
           everything; an area with zones takes every feature whose name is free
           and whose ring overlaps nothing — zones may touch along an edge, and
           identical geometry is the extreme case of overlap. A PARTIAL import
           is legal because nothing is destroyed: the preview lists every
           feature as arriving or flagged, the person confirms that subset, and
           it writes in one transaction.

           A WHOLE FILE is refused only when it cannot be read as GeoJSON, has
           no usable name property, or is projected rather than degrees.

           WHOLESALE replacement is clear-then-import: one explicit "Remove all
           N zones", never N deletions. EXPORT sits beside the import and is
           offered first in the clear confirmation. #}
        <div class="c" id="import">
            <span class="tab">Import zones<span class="src">&middot; additive</span></span>

            {% if refusal %}
                {# THE SENTENCE IS THE REASON AND NOTHING ELSE: what to do about
                   it is the next step, not what happened. #}
                <div class="upl-list">
                    <div class="upl-file bad">
                        {{ ux_icon('shell:triangle-alert') }}
                        <span class="nm">{{ refusal.file }}</span>
                        <span class="chip bad">not read</span>
                        <span class="upl-gap"></span>
                        <a class="upl-act x" href="{{ section }}" aria-label="Take this file off the zone">&times;</a>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="rln"><span class="fog">Refused</span><span class="mono">{{ refusal.why }}</span></div>
                {{ include('@Area/zone/_name_property.html.twig', {nameProperties: nameProperties}, with_context: false) }}
                <div class="pvfoot">
                    <a class="tgl" href="{{ section }}">Cancel</a>
                    <button class="cta" type="button" disabled>Add zones</button>
                </div>

            {% elseif plan %}
                {# THE PREVIEW IS THE THING THAT IS CONFIRMED, not a rehearsal of
                   the write: every feature is listed with its verdict, the
                   arriving ones are ticked, and the confirm writes what is ticked. #}
                <div class="upl-list">
                    <div class="upl-file done">
                        {{ ux_icon('shell:file-text') }}
                        <span class="nm">{{ plan.fileName }}</span>
                        <span class="sz">{{ plan.fileSizeLabel }}</span>
                        <span class="chip ok">parsed</span>
                        <span class="upl-gap"></span>
                        <a class="upl-act x" href="{{ section }}?discard=1" aria-label="Take this file off the zone">&times;</a>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="rln">
                    <span class="fog">Carries</span>
                    <span class="mono">{{ plan.count }} feature{{ plan.count == 1 ? '' : 's' }} &middot;
                        names from <b class="acc">{{ plan.nameProperty }}</b> ({{ plan.count }} of {{ plan.count }}) &middot; not stored
                        {%- if plan.skippedGeometrySummary %} &middot; skipped: {{ plan.skippedGeometrySummary }}{% endif %}
                        {%- if plan.ignoredProperties is not empty %}, all other properties{% endif %}</span>
                </div>
                <div class="rln">
                    <span class="fog">Additive</span>
                    <span class="mono">nothing here is overwritten &middot; a feature is skipped when its name exists or its ring overlaps a zone</span>
                </div>

                <form method="post" action="{{ path('area_zones_import_confirm', {uuid: area.uuidString}) }}">
                    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ importToken }}">
                    <div class="zfeats">
                        {% for feature in plan.features %}
                            <label class="zfeat{{ feature.isArriving ? '' : ' bad' }}">
                                {% if feature.isArriving %}
                                    <input type="checkbox" name="arriving[]" value="{{ feature.name }}" checked>
                                    <span class="zsw"{% if cats[feature.name] is defined %} data-cat="{{ cats[feature.name] }}"{% endif %}></span>
                                {% else %}
                                    <span class="zsw hollow"></span>
                                {% endif %}
                                {# WHAT THE FILE SAID, where the importer read it
                                   differently: a name shouted in upper case is
                                   title-cased, and this is the one place somebody
                                   still has a chance to object to that. #}
                                <span class="zfnm">{{ feature.name }}{% if feature.fileSaid %} <em class="zfwas">file said {{ feature.fileSaid }}</em>{% endif %}</span>
                                {% if feature.isArriving %}
                                    <span class="zfm">{{ feature.km2|number_format }} km&sup2;</span>
                                    <span class="chip ok">arriving</span>
                                {% else %}
                                    <span class="chip bad">flagged</span>
                                    <span class="zfwhy">{{ feature.whyLead }}{% if feature.whySubject %}<b>{{ feature.whySubject }}</b>{% endif %}{{ feature.whyTail }}</span>
                                {% endif %}
                            </label>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </div>
                    {% if set.isEmpty %}
                        <div class="rln"><span class="fog">Also</span><span class="mono">the area has no zones yet &middot; every feature arrives</span></div>
                    {% else %}
                        <div class="rln">
                            <span class="fog">On confirm</span>
                            <span class="mono">{{ plan.arriving|length }} arrive in one transaction{% if plan.flagged|length %} &middot; {{ plan.flagged|length }} skipped{% endif %}</span>
                        </div>
                    {% endif %}
                    <div class="pvfoot">
                        <a class="tgl" href="{{ section }}?discard=1">Cancel</a>
                        <button class="cta" type="submit"{{ plan.arriving|length ? '' : ' disabled' }}>Add {{ plan.arriving|length }} zone{{ plan.arriving|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }}</button>
                    </div>
                </form>

            {% else %}
                {% if outcome %}
                    <div class="zlead">
                        {{ ux_icon('shell:circle-check') }}
                        <span><b>{{ outcome.headline }}</b>{% for line in outcome.lines %} &middot; {{ line }}{% endfor %}.</span>
                    </div>
                {% endif %}

                {% if set.isEmpty %}
                    <div class="zlead">
                        {{ ux_icon('shell:upload') }}
                        <span>One polygon feature, one zone &mdash; inside the boundary, in degrees, never overlapping.</span>
                    </div>
                {% else %}
                    <div class="rln">
                        <span class="fog">The set</span>
                        <span class="mono">{{ set.count }} zone{{ set.count == 1 ? '' : 's' }}
                            {%- if set.lastImport %} &middot; last import <time datetime="{{ set.lastImport.importedAt|date('c') }}" data-localtime-format="day">{{ set.lastImport.importedAt|date('j M Y') }}</time>
                                {%- if set.lastImport.importedBy %} &middot; {{ set.lastImport.importedBy }}{% endif %}
                                &middot; names from <b class="acc">{{ set.lastImport.nameProperty }}</b>
                            {%- endif %} &middot; {{ set.zonedKm2|number_format }}{% if set.groundKm2 %} of {{ set.groundKm2|number_format }}{% endif %} km&sup2;</span>
                    </div>
                {% endif %}

                {# THE UPLOADER IS THE SHELL'S OWN `.upl-*` COMPONENT, in the mode
                   this page needs: the file is parsed and never stored. #}
                <form method="post" action="{{ path('area_zones_import_preview', {uuid: area.uuidString}) }}" enctype="multipart/form-data"
                      data-controller="uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-upload">
                    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ importToken }}">
                    <label class="upl-zone{{ set.isEmpty ? '' : ' slim' }}"
                           data-uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-upload-target="drop"
                           data-action="dragover->uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-upload#over dragleave->uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-upload#leave drop->uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-upload#drop">
                        {{ ux_icon('shell:upload') }}
                        <input type="file" name="zones" accept=".geojson,.json,application/geo+json,application/json"
                               data-uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-upload-target="file"
                               data-action="uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-upload#chosen" aria-label="Zones file">
                        <span class="lead" data-uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-upload-target="label">{% if set.isEmpty %}Drop files here, or choose one{% else %}Add more &mdash; drop a file here, or choose one{% endif %}</span>
                        <span class="upl-kinds">{% if set.isEmpty %}geojson &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; one file at a time &middot; read, never stored{% else %}geojson &middot; never stored{% endif %}</span>
                    </label>
                    {% if set.isEmpty %}{{ include('@Area/zone/_name_property.html.twig', {nameProperties: nameProperties}, with_context: false) }}{% endif %}
                    <div class="pvfoot">
                        <button class="cta" type="submit">Preview the file</button>
                    </div>
                </form>

                {% if not set.isEmpty %}
                    <div class="zsetacts">
                        <a class="btn sm" href="{{ path('area_zones_export', {uuid: area.uuidString}) }}"
                           title="{{ exportName }} &middot; FeatureCollection &middot; EPSG:4326">{{ ux_icon('shell:download') }} Export the set</a>
                        {# DESTRUCTIVE, SO IT ASKS, and the question carries the four facts
                           the design states: how many zones, how many stations fall out of
                           one, what is NOT deleted, and why past figures still add up. The
                           export sits immediately beside it, because a set nobody
                           downloaded is a set nobody can put back. #}
                        <form method="post" action="{{ path('area_zones_clear', {uuid: area.uuidString}) }}">
                            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ clearToken }}">
                            <button type="submit" class="btn sm dg"
                                    {{ stimulus_controller('confirm-modal') }}
                                    data-action="click->confirm-modal#ask"
                                    data-confirm-modal-title-value="Remove all {{ set.count }} zone{{ set.count == 1 ? '' : 's' }}?"
                                    data-confirm-modal-message-value="{{ set.count }} zone{{ set.count == 1 ? '' : 's' }} · 0 of 0 stations become unzoned. No station, person or record is deleted, and past figures regroup because they were always grouped by geometry. Download the set first: nothing keeps superseded geometry."
                                    data-confirm-modal-confirm-label-value="Remove all {{ set.count }} zone{{ set.count == 1 ? '' : 's' }}"
                                    data-confirm-modal-danger-value="true">{{ ux_icon('shell:trash-2') }} Remove all {{ set.count }} zone{{ set.count == 1 ? '' : 's' }}</button>
                        </form>
                        <span class="zfrag">one FeatureCollection &middot; EPSG:4326 &middot; names and stored properties</span>
                    </div>
                {% endif %}

                {# THE SINGLE-ZONE PATH, at rest. Drawing a ring needs a draw mode
                   on the atlas plate, which AtlasBundle does not have yet, so the
                   control is drawn as the design draws it and links nowhere. Its
                   destination is a drawing mode over the boundary and the zones in
                   AtlasBundle/assets/controllers/, writing through the same
                   ZoneService the import writes through. #}
                <div class="zdraw">
                    <button type="button" class="btn soon" disabled title="Draw a zone — coming soon">{{ ux_icon('shell:pen-tool') }} Draw a zone<span class="soonlbl">soon</span></button>
                    <span class="zfrag">adds one zone &middot; live checks &middot; stations re-read</span>
                </div>
            {% endif %}
        </div>

        {# A LOG LINE, NOT GEOMETRY: no superseded polygon is kept, so an earlier
           scheme is seen again only by importing its file again. #}
        <div class="c">
            <span class="tab">History<span class="src">&middot; newest first</span></span>
            {% if events is empty %}
                <div class="use">Nothing has happened to this area&rsquo;s zones yet. Every import, rename, ring and removal writes one line here.</div>
            {% else %}
                <div class="zhist">
                    {% for event in events %}
                        <div class="zhrow">
                            <span class="zhdot{{ event.kind.isRefusal ? ' bad' : (loop.first ? ' on' : '') }}"></span>
                            <div><b>{{ event.headline }}{% if event.detail %} <span>&middot; {{ event.detail }}</span>{% endif %}</b></div>
                            <time class="zhwhen" datetime="{{ event.occurredAt|date('c') }}" data-localtime-format="day">{{ event.occurredAt|date('j M') }}</time>
                        </div>
                    {% endfor %}
                </div>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
